⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Jati
node JTI · JTI · ⟦Jati:JTI:49588b⟧

WHO   — Jati — the thousands of birth-groups
WHAT  — The reality layer: ~3,000 castes and ~25,000 sub-castes, regional and specific — the lived unit of caste, which the four tidy varnas never mapped onto. This is what 'caste' means on the ground.
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because jati, not varna, is where caste is lived, married, and inherited — the territory under the doctrine's map.
HOW   — By birth, endogamy, hereditary occupation, and local hierarchy — negotiated and regional, not nation-wide.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am the life the doctrine only mapped — three thousand of me, each a wall around a marriage, and not one of us fits the hymn's neat four.

